---
// Request topology for a Seamless Auth deployment. Colors come from Starlight's
// theme variables so the diagram follows the light and dark themes.
---

<figure class="topology">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 800 400"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="topology-title topology-desc"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  >
    <title id="topology-title">Seamless Auth request topology</title>
    <desc id="topology-desc">
      A browser running a React app with @seamless-auth/react sends signed httpOnly cookies to your
      backend. A native app running @seamless-auth/react-native keeps its tokens in the platform
      keystore and sends them to the same backend in an Authorization Bearer header with the
      x-seamless-auth-transport bearer header. Your backend runs @seamless-auth/express, fastify or
      nextjs, and forwards each request to seamless-auth-api with a bearer token and a service
      token. The auth API owns the session, stores it in Postgres, and publishes a JWKS the backend
      uses to verify the tokens the API signs.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker
        id="topology-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="currentColor"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="10" y="30" width="190" height="120" rx="10"></rect>
      <text x="105" y="60" class="title">Browser</text>
      <text x="105" y="86">React app</text>
      <text x="105" y="106" class="mono">@seamless-auth/react</text>
      <text x="105" y="132" class="muted">holds no tokens</text>
    </g>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="10" y="240" width="190" height="120" rx="10"></rect>
      <text x="105" y="270" class="title">Native app</text>
      <text x="105" y="296" class="mono">@seamless-auth/react-native</text>
      <text x="105" y="318" class="muted">tokens in the</text>
      <text x="105" y="336" class="muted">platform keystore</text>
    </g>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="310" y="110" width="190" height="180" rx="10"></rect>
      <text x="405" y="140" class="title">Your backend</text>
      <text x="405" y="166" class="mono">@seamless-auth/express</text>
      <text x="405" y="186" class="mono">fastify, nextjs</text>
      <text x="405" y="216">/auth adapter routes</text>
      <text x="405" y="236">requireAuth</text>
      <text x="405" y="266" class="muted">keeps browser tokens</text>
      <text x="405" y="282" class="muted">in signed cookies</text>
    </g>

    <g class="box owner">
      <rect x="620" y="80" width="170" height="160" rx="10"></rect>
      <text x="705" y="110" class="title">seamless-auth-api</text>
      <text x="705" y="138" class="accent">owns the session</text>
      <text x="705" y="166">issues and</text>
      <text x="705" y="184">rotates tokens</text>
      <text x="705" y="212" class="mono">/.well-known/</text>
      <text x="705" y="228" class="mono">jwks.json</text>
    </g>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="645" y="300" width="120" height="60" rx="10"></rect>
      <text x="705" y="336" class="title">Postgres</text>
    </g>

    <g class="edge">
      <path d="M200 90 L310 160" marker-end="url(#topology-arrow)"></path>
      <path d="M200 300 L310 240" marker-end="url(#topology-arrow)"></path>
      <path d="M500 150 L620 150" marker-end="url(#topology-arrow)"></path>
      <path d="M620 220 L500 220" class="dashed" marker-end="url(#topology-arrow)"></path>
      <path d="M705 240 L705 300" marker-start="url(#topology-arrow)" marker-end="url(#topology-arrow)"></path>
    </g>

    <g class="label">
      <text x="255" y="82">signed httpOnly</text>
      <text x="255" y="98">cookies</text>
      <text x="255" y="300">Bearer tokens</text>
      <text x="255" y="316">+ transport</text>
      <text x="255" y="332">header</text>
      <text x="560" y="120">Bearer token</text>
      <text x="560" y="136">+ service token</text>
      <text x="560" y="240">JWKS verifies</text>
      <text x="560" y="256">API-signed tokens</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Both clients reach the auth API through your backend. The auth API owns the session; the
    browser and native clients differ only in where the tokens are kept.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .topology {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .topology svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }
  .topology .box rect {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .topology .owner rect {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  .topology text {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    font-size: 13px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .topology .title {
    fill: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .topology .mono {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .topology .muted {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .topology .accent {
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .topology .edge path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .topology .edge .dashed {
    stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  }
  .topology .label text {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .topology figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
